    "description": "<p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">May they be an appraiser of rare magic items, peddler of illicit substances, or bookkeeper for the court, merchants are masters of exchange.</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Iconic Merchants</strong></b></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">• Anna, Fire Emblem</span></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">• Marco Polo, Venetian merchant</span></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">• Torneko Taloon, Dragon Quest IV</span></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">• Tressa Colzione, Octopath Traveler</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Playing Merchant</strong></b></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">The merchant is a low-defense and damage character, who provides high-support through a wider inventory pool and optimizing your party’s resources. In combat, you should look out for allies in need of assistance and strategize what items to use.</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Action:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\"> Use</span></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Move:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\"> Flexible (skip to Use)</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Training: </strong></b><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Craft, Finesse, Influence</span></p>",
